title: EMR Connect › Page › Arrive and read the page
route: /emr
intro: What a person sees on arrival: the header with one button and one line saying the connection is simulated, a single 'Action required' line when something needs a person, a 'Connection health' card (four figures and one row per system) and a folded 'Advanced' section. The page follows the site view. Each region hands off to its own diagram.
dir: TD
also: Demo data, shown here for Both sites. Three systems start on the list: 'Clinical record · Site A' and 'Clinical record · Site B' (Connected) and a Billing system that serves both sites (Needs attention). A viewer who sees one site gets two rows (that site's record system and the Billing system), the title can carry a 'Site A' tag, and the figures, the Action required line and Advanced count only that site. Nothing is a real connection: 'Simulated connection' is said once, under the description.
---
start s1 "Click 'EMR Connect' in the sidebar\nUnder Connections"
screen p1 "EMR Connect\nCharts arrive on their own. Nothing is written back until a person approves it.\n'Simulated connection: this demo does not contact a real record system.'"

group gHead "Header button"
  click hb2 "Click 'Connect a system'\nA paused Reader shows a toast instead"
endgroup
goto hg2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connect a system › Choose the system and contact"
goto sg "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sites › What each site sees"

group gAct "Action required"
  screen n1 "One banner line, only when something needs a person\n'Action required: Billing system needs attention. Also: 2 fields need a mapping, so New case leaves them blank.'\nOne button for the first item: 'Fix'"
  process n2 "Nothing needs a person: no banner"
endgroup
goto ng "Continues in: EMR Connect › Page › The Action required line"

group gTiles "Four figures (not buttons)"
  process t1 "Last sync\nTime since the newest sync, and 'all systems answering'"
  process t2 "Charts matched today\n23 (Site A 13, Site B 10)"
  process t3 "Files pulled this week\n142 (Site A 80, Site B 62)"
  process t4 "Sync failures\n2, from the Billing system (it serves both sites, so each site view shows the same 2)"
endgroup
goto tg "Continues in: EMR Connect › Page › What the health figures show"

group gSys "Connection health"
  screen c1 "Connection health\n'2 of 3 systems connected. Read access for charts, insurance details and medications.'\nOne site: 'Site A. 1 of 2 systems connected...' and, for a one-site viewer, an info icon on why only some systems show"
  process c2 "One row per system: name, status pill, what it holds and reads ('All programs at Site A. Reads ...'), last sync, sync failures, buttons\nThen a line: 'Read only' or 'Read and write back', with the Write back switch"
  click c3 "Click 'Sync now' in the card header"
  click c4 "Click 'Sync now', 'Fix', 'Reconnect' or 'Manage' on a row\nA row that is not Connected also says that New case cannot pull a chart from it"
  click c6 "Click the 'Write back' switch on a row"
  toast c5 "'Connect your record system to let charts arrive on their own.'\nEmpty list. Not reachable in the demo: a system can be disconnected, never removed"
endgroup
goto cg0 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sync › When an agent is paused or asks first"
goto cg1 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Sync › Sync now"
goto cg2 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connected systems › What each status means"
goto cg3 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Problems › Every error state and what it needs"
goto cg4 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Connected systems › Read only or read and write back"
goto cg5 "Continues in: EMR Connect › Manage › Open the Manage drawer"

group gAdv "Advanced (folded)"
  screen a1 "Advanced\n'10 field mappings, 2 waiting, and the log of every read and write (8 lines).'\nPill '2 to map'\nFor one site the counts are that site's: Site A '7 field mappings ... (5 lines)', Site B '5 field mappings, 2 waiting ... (3 lines)'"
  click a2 "Click 'Advanced', or Tab to it and press Enter or Space"
endgroup
goto ag "Continues in: EMR Connect › Advanced › Field mappings and the activity log"

s1 --> p1
p1 --> hb2
hb2 --> hg2
p1 -.-> sg
p1 --> n1
p1 -.-> n2
n1 --> ng
p1 --> t1 & t2 & t3 & t4
t1 --> tg
t2 --> tg
t3 --> tg
t4 --> tg
p1 --> c1
c1 --> c2
c2 --> c3 & c4 & c6
c1 -.-> c5
c3 --> cg1
c3 -.-> cg0
c4 -.-> cg0
c4 --> cg2
c4 -.-> cg3
c4 --> cg5
c6 --> cg4
p1 --> a1
a1 --> a2 --> ag
